Explanation:
Both Field_1 and Field_2 have the highest bird‐threat level (0.15). Field_2 already has four drones assigned (two protecting and two en route), so we leave them in place to maintain its full protection. Field_1 currently has no protection, so to meet its requirement of four drones we reassign the remaining available drones – those that are idle (Drone_5 and Drone_6) and those still in transit to Field_3 (Drone_2 and Drone_8). Although Field_3 (threat 0.11) would lose its protection by this reassignment, protecting the most endangered fields (with threat 0.15) remains our top priority. This allocation minimizes overall damage by ensuring that both highest‐threat fields are fully covered.
